    --interval 1d \
    --date-range 14d \
    --filter channel=search
```
```curl
curl -G 'https://<REGION>.cloud.appwrite.io/v1/analytics/properties/<PROPERTY_ID>/metrics' \
    -H 'X-Appwrite-Project: <PROJECT_ID>' \
    -H 'X-Appwrite-Key: <API_KEY>' \
    --data-urlencode 'interval=1d' \
    --data-urlencode 'dateRange=14d' \
    --data-urlencode 'queries[]={"method":"equal","attribute":"channel","values":["search"]}'
```
{% /multicode %}

Every dimension except `entryPage` and `exitPage` works as a filter, and `props.<key>`, such as `props.plan`, filters on a prop's value. `trafficType` takes `human` or `bot` with `equal` or `notEqual`.

Filters on `page`, `eventName`, `userId`, and `props.<key>` match single events, so they work only with `interval` or with a breakdown other than `entryPage` and `exitPage`. Totals don't accept them, because totals cover whole visits.
